# CODEOWNERS — starter. Copy to a PLATFORM-RECOGNIZED path and fill with REAL owners.
# Platform-AGNOSTIC: the CODEOWNERS format is shared across GitHub / GitLab / Gitea (Bitbucket uses its
# own "default reviewers" instead). The recognized PATH and the protection setting differ per platform —
# verify yours; do NOT assume GitHub.
#
# [!] INERT WITHOUT PROTECTION. This file ALONE enforces nothing. To actually hold:
#     1. place it at a path your platform recognizes — commonly a repo-root `CODEOWNERS`, or under
#        `.github/` (GitHub), `.gitlab/` (GitLab), `.gitea/` (Gitea), or `docs/`; AND
#     2. configure the platform so the protected branch REQUIRES review/approval from the owners
#        (GitHub: branch protection "require review from Code Owners"; GitLab: protected branch +
#        "Code Owner approval required"; Gitea: branch protection "enable code owners"; others vary).
#     Without step 2 it is advisory decoration. A LOCAL git / agent hook CANNOT enforce review ownership
#     across other actors — only the remote platform can. (See `repo-collaboration`, principle 2.)
#
# Owners are REAL platform identities or teams with write access (`@user`, `@org/team`) — not prose names.
# PRECEDENCE is platform-dependent: on GitHub / GitLab / Gitea the LAST matching pattern wins, so put the
# broad fallback FIRST and specific overrides LATER — but VERIFY for your platform. One rule per line:
# `<path-glob>  <owner> [<owner>...]`.
#
# [!] Required review can DEADLOCK (a PR/MR left waiting). Pair it with an escalation valve
#     (see `repo-collaboration` — "review starvation"): agree a wait, then ping / split / arbitrate;
#     never bypass the guard to beat the wait.

